  "summary": {
    "plain": "A later study of the AMoRE-Pilot backgrounds, which identified their sources across three configurations, gives a half-life limit of 3.0 x 10^23 years (90% confidence) for neutrinoless double beta decay of molybdenum-100.",
    "technical": "Pilot stage with ~1.9 kg CaMoO4 at Y2L from 2015 to 2018; the limit is derived from the measured background and its Monte Carlo model (arXiv preprint; no journal reference in the abstract page)."
